WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.380
data, when you look at the hydradenitis superativa NBRX naive share, you can see here pretty

00:00:06.380 --> 00:00:14.020
consistently around 50%. We did see a slight dip in January because of the re-verification

00:00:14.020 --> 00:00:19.720
and the availability of biosimilars. We see that now climbing back up. So we expect to be stable

00:00:19.720 --> 00:00:26.100
in that 50% range. Importantly as well for IV patient share, we see steady growth up to now

00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:31.460
14%. And so both of these will continue to be important. We are hoping that the HS market

00:00:31.460 --> 00:00:36.520
continues to develop, not just for cosentics, but as we'll address later, remirutinib now

00:00:36.520 --> 00:00:42.040
will also have a readout later this year in HS. So we want to see this market expand so the patients

00:00:42.040 --> 00:00:47.980
who need better therapies are getting them. Outside of the US, we were up 3%. That's

00:00:47.980 --> 00:00:49.700
primarily driven by growth in Europe. We're up 3% in the U.S. and we're up 3% in the U.S.

00:00:49.720 --> 00:00:55.060
and emerging markets. We continue to see competitive pressures in China with multiple

00:00:55.060 --> 00:01:01.300
local NRDL entrants. And so there's a long list of competitors that we have. And we've had very

00:01:01.300 --> 00:01:05.880
strong share performance in China now over many years, but our goal will be to maintain now

00:01:05.880 --> 00:01:10.760
share and hopefully can stabilize as well the performance in China over the coming quarters.

00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:15.080
We continue to advance the new indications. Importantly, the PMR submission,

00:01:15.080 --> 00:01:19.700
it happened across geographies and we expect the FDA approval in the second half.

00:01:19.720 --> 00:01:26.200
And we also received FDA approval for the pediatric HS indication, and we completed EMA

00:01:26.200 --> 00:01:32.740
submission as well. So all on track on that front. So moving to slide 12, I wanted to just say a few

00:01:32.740 --> 00:01:37.840
words on our renal portfolio by talking about each of the key brands. So first, let's talk about

00:01:37.840 --> 00:01:47.560
Fabhalta. Sales were up 103% in quarter one with NBRX leadership now, both in PNH and C3G. In PNH,

00:01:49.720 --> 00:01:55.240
NBRX share, as well as important and significant contributions from some of our key ex-US markets.

00:01:55.240 --> 00:02:03.340
In C3G, 56% NBRX share, and we're now approved in 46 countries. So both of those indications really

00:02:03.340 --> 00:02:08.500
having solid and consistent performance. Now importantly, in IGAN, I think we believe our

00:02:08.500 --> 00:02:14.080
uptake in US patients will continue to build and with patients with persistent proteinuria

00:02:14.080 --> 00:02:19.660
and glomerular inflammation. So here we're at later line therapy. But I think very

